    <h1 style="color:#0f1f3d;">Truck Batteries for the Southeast Asian Market</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Southeast Asia is a core JIS market — Japanese and Korean heavy trucks dominate regional
      fleets, running JIS N-series batteries. DINWEYS stocks the full N100&ndash;N200 range, built for
      the region's heat and humidity.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:20px 0;padding:16px 20px;background:#f4f7fb;border-left:4px solid #f5a623;border-radius:6px;">
      <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin:0 0 10px;font-size:1.15rem;">Direct Answer</h2>
      <p style="margin:0;">Southeast Asia's commercial fleet is overwhelmingly Japanese — Hino, Isuzu, Mitsubishi Fuso and UD Trucks dominate, with Hino holding roughly 56% of Indonesia's medium-duty segment — so the battery standard is JIS, with N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52) as the heavy-truck workhorses and N100/N120 below them for light and medium duty. The climate is tropical year-round (typically 25&ndash;32&deg;C with 70&ndash;90% humidity), which stresses batteries through heat plus terminal corrosion. Imports clear through country-specific conformity — SNI (Indonesia), SIRIM (Malaysia), TISI (Thailand) — with Singapore, Port Klang, Laem Chabang and Tanjung Priok as the main gateways.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Market Overview</h2>
    <p>
      Indonesia — the region's largest market — has a commercial-vehicle market expected to reach
      <strong>USD 11.32&nbsp;billion (2025)</strong>, growing at a 4.97% CAGR to about USD 14.43&nbsp;billion
      by 2030, with Hino Motors, Isuzu Motors, Daimler Commercial Vehicles (Mercedes-Benz), UD Trucks
      and Mitsubishi Fuso Truck &amp; Bus as the major companies
      (<a href="https://www.mordorintelligence.com/industry-reports/indonesia-commercial-vehicle-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mordor Intelligence</a>).
      Hino has held the market-leader position in Indonesia's medium-duty truck segment for 25
      consecutive years, citing about 56% share in 2025
      (<a href="https://www.hino.co.id/news-detail/528/hino-pertahankan-posisi-market-leader-medium-duty-truck-selama-25-tahun-raih-56-pangsa-pasar-di-2025" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Hino Indonesia</a>).
      The box-truck segment lists Mitsubishi Fuso, Isuzu, Hino, Toyota and Daihatsu as major companies
      (<a href="https://www.kenresearch.com/industry-reports/indonesia-box-truck-market" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ken Research</a>).
    </p>
    <p>
      The precise installed-fleet split by brand across all ASEAN markets is not published in a single
      official source, so treat the mix above as structure rather than exact share.
      <em>Precise brand share: Not publicly verified.</em>
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Climate &amp; Duty Demands</h2>
    <p>
      Southeast Asia has a tropical climate characterized by warm temperatures year-round — typically
      <strong>25&ndash;32&deg;C</strong> — with high humidity between <strong>70% and 90%</strong> and abundant
      monsoon rainfall
      (<a href="https://www.thai-aec.com/southeast-asia-climate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Thai-AEC — Southeast Asia climate</a>;
      <a href="https://seasia.co/2025/05/20/from-floods-to-frost-the-wild-weather-of-southeast-asia" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Seasia — weather of Southeast Asia</a>).
      Most of the region is tropical monsoon or tropical rainforest, with the heat and humidity
      stressing batteries in two ways at once.
    </p>
    <p>
      Heat accelerates the chemical reactions that age plates and increases electrolyte water loss in
      flooded designs. Humidity promotes corrosion on terminals and connections, which raises
      resistance and reduces cranking current. The practical answer for buyers is a thick-plate (Pb-Sb)
      flooded construction with clean, tight terminals, or a sealed AGM option that resists corrosion
      better than a vented flooded design.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Vehicle Mix &amp; Common Battery Groups</h2>
    <p>
      The group follows the vehicle. Japanese trucks — Hino 500/700 and Ranger, Isuzu Forward/F-Series,
      Mitsubishi Fuso Fighter/Super Great, UD Quon and Nissan Diesel Condor — are specified in JIS
      N-series codes. The heavy-truck workhorse is <strong>N150</strong> (145G51, 508 &times; 222 &times;
      212&nbsp;mm), with <strong>N200</strong> (190H52, 520 &times; 278 &times; 220&nbsp;mm) for the largest
      engines. Below them, N100 and N120 serve light and medium trucks (Hino Dutro, Isuzu Elf, Fuso
      Canter). Aftermarket listings across Malaysia and the region fit the N150 group to Hino, Isuzu,
      Nissan, Volvo, Scania, Fuso and Howo trucks. The groups that dominate Southeast Asian fleets:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Battery group</th><th>DINWEYS model</th><th>Capacity / CCA</th><th>Typical vehicle class</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>JIS N150</td><td>145G51</td><td>135 Ah · 900 A (JIS)</td><td>Heavy trucks, buses, semi-trailers</td></tr>
        <tr><td>JIS N200</td><td>190H52</td><td>200 Ah · 1100 A (JIS)</td><td>Largest engines, high-load buses</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="data-note">
      Group-to-vehicle mapping is a third-party fitment reference — a compatible reference, not a
      DINWEYS OEM confirmation. Confirm dimensions, terminal layout and voltage against the specific
      truck before ordering.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Standards</h2>
    <p>
      Japanese and Korean heavy trucks — the dominant makes in Southeast Asia — use JIS (Japanese
      Industrial Standards) sizing, with model codes N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52) the workhorses
      of commercial fleets. Importers should specify JIS rather than China's domestic GB reference
      codes to match local aftermarket demand and terminal conventions. Match the battery to the
      vehicle's group, dimensions and terminal orientation. For a technical comparison, see
      <a href="/compare/jis-vs-din-vs-bci/" style="color:#1e5aa8;">JIS vs DIN vs BCI</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">DINWEYS Relevance</h2>
    <p>
      DINWEYS — manufactured by Chengguang Power Tech Co., Ltd. — carries the JIS N-series heavy-truck
      groups that dominate Southeast Asian fleets in one line: N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52), the
      region's core commercial batteries. These are positioned as
      <strong>compatible references</strong> matched by group, dimensions and CCA — not as OEM
      replacements — so a distributor can cover the region's Japanese-dominated fleet from a single
      manufacturer and a single shipment.
    </p>

    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Buyer Considerations</h2>
    <ol class="takeaways-list">
      <li><strong>Specify JIS, not GB.</strong> JIS N-series (N100/N120/N150/N200) is the core commercial range across Southeast Asia, matching local Japanese/Korean trucks and terminal conventions. Specify JIS to match local aftermarket demand.</li>
      <li><strong>Account for heat plus humidity.</strong> Tropical temperatures of 25&ndash;32&deg;C with 70&ndash;90% humidity accelerate ageing and promote terminal corrosion. Thick-plate flooded construction with clean, tight terminals — or sealed AGM — extends service life.</li>
      <li><strong>Clear conformity before shipment.</strong> Schemes vary by country — SNI (Indonesia), SIRIM (Malaysia), TISI (Thailand) and the PS mark (Philippines) are examples. Confirm the current scheme and labelling with your importer.</li>
      <li><strong>Plan the port.</strong> Singapore and Port Klang (Malaysia) are the region's transshipment hubs; Laem Chabang (Thailand), Tanjung Priok (Jakarta) and Manila serve local distribution. Choose the gateway nearest your market.</li>
    </ol>

