    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does Southeast Asia use for trucks?</h3>
      <p>Southeast Asia is a core JIS market — Japanese and Korean heavy trucks dominate, running JIS N-series batteries in model codes N150 (145G51) and N200 (190H52), with lighter N100/N120 for light and medium trucks. Match the battery to the vehicle.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why is JIS the safe spec for Southeast Asia?</h3>
      <p>JIS N-series (N100/N120/N150/N200) is the core commercial range across Southeast Asia, matching local Japanese/Korean trucks and their terminal conventions. Importers should specify JIS rather than China's domestic GB codes to match local aftermarket demand.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
